*****************************************************************
* DALYTRAN-VALID.dat - Valid daily transaction test data
* Layout: CVTRA06Y.cpy (DALYTRAN-RECORD, 350 bytes per record)
*
* Field layout (350 bytes total):
*   DALYTRAN-ID              PIC X(16)     Pos 1-16
*   DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD         PIC X(02)     Pos 17-18
*   DALYTRAN-CAT-CD          PIC 9(04)     Pos 19-22
*   DALYTRAN-SOURCE          PIC X(10)     Pos 23-32
*   DALYTRAN-DESC            PIC X(100)    Pos 33-132
*   DALYTRAN-AMT             PIC S9(09)V99 Pos 133-143 (signed)
*   DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID     PIC 9(09)     Pos 144-152
*   DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME   PIC X(50)     Pos 153-202
*   DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY   PIC X(50)     Pos 203-252
*   DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP    PIC X(10)     Pos 253-262
*   DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM        PIC X(16)     Pos 263-278
*   DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS         PIC X(26)     Pos 279-304
*   DALYTRAN-PROC-TS         PIC X(26)     Pos 305-330
*   FILLER                   PIC X(20)     Pos 331-350
*
* Records:
*   1: Valid purchase - card 4000123456789010, $100.00
*   2: Valid purchase - card 4000123456789010, $500.00
*   3: Credit/refund  - card 4000123456789010, -$50.00
*
* NOTE: The actual .dat file is generated by the test script
*       using the data generation program or manually created
*       to match the exact EBCDIC/ASCII layout needed by the
*       target platform (GnuCOBOL or mainframe).
*****************************************************************
